{"instruction": "Write q code that create a q/kdb+ function checkargs to validate data", "input": "", "output": "checkargs:{[args;k;t]\n \t$[not 99h~type args;'`$\"Input parameter must be a dictionary with keys:\\n\\t-\",sv[\"\\n\\t-\";string k];  / - check for dictionary\n        / - check for keys\n        not all k in key[args];'`$\"Dictionary keys are incorrect. Keys should be:\\n\\t-\", sv[\"\\n\\t-\";string k], \"\\nYou have input keys:\\n\\t-\", sv[\"\\n\\t-\";string key args];\n        / - check for types\n\t\t/ any not in'[string .Q.ty'[args k];t]\n        any not .Q.ty'[args k] in t;'`$(\"One or more of your inputs are of an invalid type.\");\n        `table in key args;\n        / - check if columns are in table provided\n        (if[any not args[`keycols] in cols args`table;'`$(\"The columns (\", raze string args[`keycols],\") you are attempting to use does not exist in the table provided.\")]);\n        :()]\n    }"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function savetabdata to group data by key columns", "input": "", "output": "savetabdata:{[h;p;t;data;UPSERT;td]\n $[partandmerge;path:pathtotable[td;p;t];path:pathtotable[h;p;t]];\n if[not partandmerge;.lg.o[`replay;\"saving table \",(string t),\" to \",string path]];\n .replay.pathlist[t],:path;\n $[partandmerge;savetablesbypart[td;p;t;h];$[UPSERT;upsert;set] . (path;.Q.en[h;0!.save.manipulate[t;data]])]\n  }"}
