{"instruction": "Show me how to implement setserverstate in q/kdb+ using qSQL", "input": "", "output": "setserverstate:{[serverh;usestate] \n $[usestate;\n   update inuse:usestate,lastquery:.proc.cp[],querycount+1i from `.gw.servers where handle in serverh;\n   update inuse:usestate,usage:usage+.proc.cp[] - lastquery from `.gw.servers where handle in serverh]}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function generateschemas that group data by key columns for a trading system in a tick database", "input": "", "output": "generateschemas:{\n  .stpps.init[tables[] except `currlog`heartbeat`logmsg`svrstoload];\n  .stpps.attrstrip[.stpps.t];\n\n  // Table UPD functions attach the current timestamp by default, if STP is chained these do nothing\n  $[.sctp.chainedtp;\n    .stplg.updtab:(.stpps.t!(count .stpps.t)#{[x;y] x}"}
{"instruction": "What's the q code for write q code for reload to load data from files or databases", "input": "", "output": "reload:{\n\t.lg.o[`reload;\"reloading HDB\"];\n\tsystem\"l .\"}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for substituteLine to perform data operations for a trading system using qSQL", "input": "", "output": "substituteLine:{[d;l];\n  pred:(p[0] < p[1]) and 2 = count p: first flip l ss/: (\"%(\";\")s\");\n  if[() ~ pred;:l]; / If there are no substitution characters, p is an empty list and the normal predicate doesn't work right\n  $[pred;\n    $[(lookup:2 _ (pieces:(0,p) cut l) 1) in key d;\n      .z.s[d;pieces[0],d[lookup],2 _ pieces 2];\n      not \"\" ~ e:getenv `$lookup;\n      .z.s[d;pieces[0],e,2 _ pieces 2];\n      l\n      ];\n    l / The substitution strings were in the wrong order or there was only one and there was no substitution to perform\n    ]\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for query_554 to execute a query and return results in a production environment", "input": "", "output": "exec name from .api.detail)?api`name}\n\n// get all the namespaces in . form\nallns:{`$(enlist enlist \".\"),\".\",/:string key `}\n\n// Dump out everything across all name spaces\nfullapi:{\n\tres:`name xkey raze list .' allns[] cross key typemap"}
