{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that group data by key columns", "input": "", "output": "symwcheck:{[size]\n    .checks.errs::();\n\n    if [(h:.Q.w[]`symw) > size;\n        .checks.errs,:\"This process exceeded the warning for symbol size of \",numformat[size],\" bytes at \",timeformat[],\"<br />\";\n        .checks.errs,:\"The output of .Q.w[] for this process has been listed below.<br/><br/>\";\n\t.checks.errs,:formatdict .Q.w[]];\n\n    ([]messages:.checks.errs)}"}
{"instruction": "I need to write q code for reruncheck to filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "reruncheck:{[chkid]\n  .lg.o[`dqc;\"rerunning check \",string chkid];\n  d:exec action, params, proc from .dqe.configtable where checkid=chkid;\n  .lg.o[`dqc;\"re-running check \",(string d`action),\" manually\"];\n  d[`params]:value d[`params] 0;\n  d[`proc]:value raze d`proc;\n  /- input man argument is `manual or `scheduled indicating manul run is on or off\n  .dqe.runcheck[`manual;chkid;.Q.dd[`.dqc;d`action];d`params;d`proc];\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Using qSQL, Write a q function named upd that perform data operations for a trading system for financial data", "input": "", "output": "upd:{[t;x]ts .z.p;\n a:.z.p+.eodtime.dailyadj; \n if[not -12=type first first x;\n     /a:\"n\"$a;\n     x:$[0>type first x;\n         a,x;\n         (enlist(count first x)#a),x\n         ]\n     ];\n f:key flip value t;pub[t;$[0>type first x;enlist f!x;flip f!x]];if[l;l enlist (`upd;t;x);i+:1;icounts[t]+::count first x];}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function end that perform data operations for financial data", "input": "", "output": "end:{\n  (neg allsubhandles[])@\\:(`endofday;x;y);\n }"}
{"instruction": "I need to write a q function that perform data operations for a trading system", "input": "", "output": "notifyhdb:{[dir;h]\n  .lg.o[`dqc;\"notifying the hdb to reload\"];\n  /- if you can connect to the hdb - call the reload function\n  @[h;\"system \\\"l \",dir,\"\\\"\";{.lg.e[`notifyhdb;\"failed to send reload message to hdb on handle: \",x]}"}
{"instruction": "What's the q code for implement a function badmsg that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "badmsg:{[e;t;x]\n  .lg.o[`upd;\"Bad message received, error: \",e];\n  `..loghandles[errorlogname] enlist(`upderr;t;x);\n }"}
{"instruction": "In q/kdb+, Implement a function olddir that perform data operations for a trading system for a trading system", "input": "", "output": "olddir:{[logdir]\n  .replay.segmentedmode:0b;\n  .replay.tplogfile:`;\n  .replay.tplogdir:logdir;\n  .replay.initandrun[];\n }"}
{"instruction": "Using qSQL, Create a q/kdb+ function connectcustom to execute a query and return results in a production environment", "input": "", "output": "connectcustom:{[connectiontab] \n .lg.o[`monitor;\"created outgoing connections\"];\n subscribe each (exec w from connectiontab) except subscribedhandles;\n }"}
{"instruction": "In q/kdb+, Show me how to implement togglecheck in q/kdb+ for financial data", "input": "", "output": "togglecheck:{[cid;status]\n  if[not cid in exec checkid from checkconfig; '\"checkid \",(string cid),\" doesn't exist\"];\n  update active:status from `checkconfig where checkid=cid;\n }"}
{"instruction": "How do I calculate aggregate statistics", "input": "", "output": "find:{[path;match;exclude;age;agemin;checkfordirectory]\n\t$[0=checkfordirectory;[fileordir:\"files\";flag:\"f\"];[fileordir:\"directories\";flag:\"d\"]];\n\tdayormin:$[0=agemin;\"mtime\";\"mmin\"];\n\tfindmatches:{[path;match;exclude;age;fileordir;flag;dayormin]\n\t\t\t.lg.o[`housekeeping;\"Searching for \",fileordir,\": \",path,match];\n\t\t\t.proc.sys \"/usr/bin/find \",path,\" -maxdepth 1 -type \",flag,\" -name \\\"\",match,\"\\\" -\",dayormin,\" +\",(raze string age),\" ! -name \\\"\",exclude,\"\\\"\"}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that process incoming data in a tick database", "input": "", "output": "processDefReg:{[flags;typ;default;handler];\n  val:arg.filterVals arg.getRegOpt each arg.filterFlags flags;\n  $[count val;\n    arg.setReg[typ;handler;1b;val];\n    arg.setReg[typ;handler;0b;default]\n    ];\n  }"}
{"instruction": "What's the q code for create a q/kdb+ function savetabdata to group data by key columns for a trading system", "input": "", "output": "savetabdata:{[h;p;t;data;UPSERT;td]\n $[partandmerge;path:pathtotable[td;p;t];path:pathtotable[h;p;t]];\n if[not partandmerge;.lg.o[`replay;\"saving table \",(string t),\" to \",string path]];\n .replay.pathlist[t],:path;\n $[partandmerge;savetablesbypart[td;p;t;h];$[UPSERT;upsert;set] . (path;.Q.en[h;0!.save.manipulate[t;data]])]\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function extractkeys to perform data operations using qSQL", "input": "", "output": "extractkeys:{[queryparams;k]\n  k:k inter key queryparams;\n  :raze queryparams k;\n  }"}
{"instruction": "In q/kdb+, Write a q function named bind that perform data operations in a tick database", "input": "", "output": "bind:{[sess;customDict]\n  defaultKeys:`dn`cred`mech;\n  defaultVals:```;\n  defaultDict:defaultKeys!defaultVals;\n  if[customDict~(::);customDict:()!()];\n  if[99h<>type customDict;'\"customDict must be (::) or a dictionary\"];\n  updDict:defaultDict,customDict;\n  bindSession:.ldap.bind_s[sess;;;]. updDict defaultKeys;\n  bindSession\n  }"}
